==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|envigorate}}
* {{l|en|envigourate}} {{qualifier|rare}}
* {{l|en|invigourate}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪnˈvɪɡəɹeɪt/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|invigorat}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To impart [[vigor]], [[strength]], or [[vitality]] to.
#: ''Exercise is '''invigorating'''.''
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[heighten]] or [[intensify]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To give life or energy to.
#: ''The cold water '''invigorated''' him.''
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make [[lively]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to impart vigor, strength, or vitality}} See also [[Thesaurus:strengthen]]

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|invigorating}}
* {{l|en|invigoratingly}}
* {{l|en|invigoration}}
* {{l|en|invigorator}}

